= $dots$
This course acts as an introduction to the path integral formalism of quantum field theory. There is no assumed background on quantum field theory.#footnote[The depth of the covered material is thus lacking during certain parts, and mathematical details or pedantics are ignored at will.]

We loosely follow the IAS notes on quantum field theory by Witten and Faddeev, as well as the notes on quantum field theory by Etingof.

